<browser_guidelines>
- When researching documentation or reading articles, always use Tier 1 lightweight tool: `read_url_content(url)` or `search_web(query, max_results, domain)`.
- When interacting with live applications, SPAs, or debugging UI via `chrome-devtools` (connected through the Local CDP Hub on `127.0.0.1:19222`):
  1. Use `navigate_page(url)` to load the site.
  2. Use `take_snapshot()` to retrieve the Accessibility Tree.
  3. Locate the target element and its numeric `uid`.
  4. Perform actions via `click(uid)` or `fill(uid, value)`.
  5. Check `take_screenshot(filePath)` or `list_console_messages()` to verify UI changes and detect errors — always pass `filePath` (avoids the 30s IPC timeout); keep Chrome unminimized.
- For multi-account or parallel sessions in the same Chrome window, use `tether-containers` (`list_containers`, `create_container`, `open_container_page`, `clear_container`) or `new_page(url, background, isolatedContext)` and pass `pageId` to all page tools.
</browser_guidelines>
